* opamp_1p.lib
* Behavioral single-pole op-amp model, compatible with LTspice and ngspice.
*
*   Open-loop DC gain  A0  = 1e5  (100 dB)
*   Gain-bandwidth     GBW = 1 MHz  ->  dominant pole fp = GBW / A0 = 10 Hz
*   Output clamped to the supply rails (single supply 0-5 V in this project)
*
* Pin order matches the LTspice "opamp2" symbol:  In+  In-  V+  V-  OUT
*
* Not modelled: input offset voltage, input bias current, noise, slew rate,
* output current limit, finite output resistance.

.subckt opamp_1p inp inn vcc vee out
* Transconductance stage: 1 mS into 100 Meg = 1e5 V/V DC gain
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1m
R1 n1 0 100Meg
* Dominant pole: fp = 1 / (2*pi*R1*C1) = 10 Hz
C1 n1 0 159.155p
* Output buffer, clamped to the rails
B1 out 0 V=max(min(V(n1), V(vcc)), V(vee))
.ends opamp_1p
